@ref Criminal Code s 63 (unlawful assembly) (src:1060-1067)
GIVEN `the number of persons assembled` IS A NUMBER
      `the persons assemble with intent to carry out a common purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the persons assemble in such a manner, or so conduct themselves when assembled, as to cause persons in the neighbourhood of the assembly to fear` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fear is on reasonable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fear is that they will disturb the peace tumultuously` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fear is that they will by that assembly needlessly and without reasonable cause provoke other persons to disturb the peace tumultuously` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the persons are lawfully assembled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the persons conduct themselves with a common purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the persons are assembled to protect the dwelling-house of any one of them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 dwelling-house: the place is a dwelling-house` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the persons they protect it against are threatening to break and enter it for the purpose of committing an indictable offence therein` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that is the only reason they could be unlawfully assembled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63 the persons are unlawfully assembled` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 63(3) the persons are unlawfully assembled by reason only that they are assembled to protect a dwelling-house` `the persons are assembled to protect the dwelling-house of any one of them` `s 2 dwelling-house: the place is a dwelling-house` `the persons they protect it against are threatening to break and enter it for the purpose of committing an indictable offence therein` `that is the only reason they could be unlawfully assembled` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Persons are not unlawfully assembled by reason only that they are assembled to protect the dwelling-house of any one of them" (subsection (3))
        IF `s 63(1) the assembly is an unlawful assembly` `the number of persons assembled` `the persons assemble with intent to carry out a common purpose` `the persons assemble in such a manner, or so conduct themselves when assembled, as to cause persons in the neighbourhood of the assembly to fear` `the fear is on reasonable grounds` `the fear is that they will disturb the peace tumultuously` `the fear is that they will by that assembly needlessly and without reasonable cause provoke other persons to disturb the peace tumultuously` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 63(2) persons who are lawfully assembled may become an unlawful assembly` `the persons are lawfully assembled` `the persons conduct themselves with a common purpose` (`s 63(1) the assembly is an unlawful assembly` `the number of persons assembled` `the persons assemble with intent to carry out a common purpose` `the persons assemble in such a manner, or so conduct themselves when assembled, as to cause persons in the neighbourhood of the assembly to fear` `the fear is on reasonable grounds` `the fear is that they will disturb the peace tumultuously` `the fear is that they will by that assembly needlessly and without reasonable cause provoke other persons to disturb the peace tumultuously`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An unlawful assembly is an assembly of three or more persons who" (subsection (1), a definition; subsection (2) does not reach the case)

§ `Section 64 -- Riot`

-- src:1068 | Riot
-- src:1069 | 64 A riot is an unlawful assembly that has begun to disturb the peace tumultuously.
@ref Criminal Code s 64 (riot) (src:1068-1069)
GIVEN `s 63 the persons are unlawfully assembled: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the unlawful assembly has begun to disturb the peace tumultuously` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64 the unlawful assembly is a riot` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the unlawful assembly has begun to disturb the peace tumultuously` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A riot is an unlawful assembly that has begun to disturb the peace tumultuously"
        IF `s 63 the persons are unlawfully assembled: the answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A riot is an unlawful assembly"
        IF `s 63 the persons are unlawfully assembled: the answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): section 63 does not answer

§ `Sections 65 and 66 -- Punishment of rioter, punishment for unlawful assembly`

-- src:1070 | Punishment of rioter
-- src:1071 | 65 (1) Every person who takes part in a riot is guilty of
-- src:1072 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:1073 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 65(1) (punishment of rioter) (src:1070-1073)
GIVEN `the person takes part in the riot` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 64 the unlawful assembly is a riot: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65(1) the person takes part in a riot` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 64 the unlawful assembly is a riot: the answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A riot is an unlawful assembly that has begun to disturb the peace tumultuously" (section 64)
        IF `the person takes part in the riot` AND `s 64 the unlawful assembly is a riot: the answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who takes part in a riot"

@ref Criminal Code s 65(1) (punishment of rioter) (src:1070-1073)
`s 65(1) the class of the offence of taking part in a riot` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 65(1) (punishment of rioter) (src:1070-1073)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 65(1) the punishment for taking part in a riot` MEANS
    LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

