§ `Section 67 -- Reading proclamation`

-- "A person who is (a) a justice, mayor or sheriff, or the lawful deputy of a mayor or sheriff, (b) a warden or deputy warden of a prison, or (c) the institutional head of a penitentiary, ... or that person's
-- deputy, who receives notice that, at any place within the jurisdiction of the person, twelve or more persons are unlawfully and riotously assembled together shall go to that place and, after approaching as
-- near as is safe, if the person is satisfied that a riot is in progress, shall command silence and thereupon make or cause to be made in a loud voice a proclamation in the following words or to the like effect:"
-- The persons named are officials: the section is encoded for what it decides (when the duty arises, and what follows for the persons assembled: see section 68). The core's Party type has no constructor for a
-- mayor, a sheriff, a warden or an institutional head, so the section's own offices are a type of this module (NEEDS-CORE.md).
-- src:1084 | Reading proclamation
-- src:1085 | 67 A person who is
-- src:1086 | (a) a justice, mayor or sheriff, or the lawful deputy of a mayor or sheriff,
-- src:1087 | (b) a warden or deputy warden of a prison, or
-- src:1088 | (c) the institutional head of a penitentiary, as those expressions are defined in subsection 2(1) of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act, or that person’s deputy,
-- src:1089 | who receives notice that, at any place within the jurisdiction of the person, twelve or more persons are unlawfully and riotously assembled together shall go to that place and, after approaching as near as is safe, if the person is satisfied that a riot is in progress, shall command silence and thereupon make or cause to be made in a loud voice a proclamation in the following words or to the like effect:
@ref Criminal Code s 67 (reading proclamation) (src:1084-1089)
DECLARE `s 67 office` IS ONE OF
    `s 67(a) a justice`
    `s 67(a) a mayor`
    `s 67(a) a sheriff`
    `s 67(a) the lawful deputy of a mayor or sheriff`
    `s 67(b) a warden of a prison`
    `s 67(b) a deputy warden of a prison`
    `s 67(c) the institutional head of a penitentiary`
    `s 67(c) the deputy of the institutional head of a penitentiary`
    `s 67 another office`

@ref Criminal Code s 67 (reading proclamation) (src:1084-1089)
GIVEN office IS A `s 67 office`
      `the person receives notice that, at a place within the person's jurisdiction, persons are unlawfully and riotously assembled together` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of persons the notice says are assembled` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67 the person must go to that place` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF office EQUALS `s 67 another office` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is (a) a justice, mayor or sheriff ... (b) a warden or deputy warden of a prison, or (c) the institutional head of a penitentiary"
        IF NOT `the person receives notice that, at a place within the person's jurisdiction, persons are unlawfully and riotously assembled together` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who receives notice that, at any place within the jurisdiction of the person"
        IF `the number of persons the notice says are assembled` LESS THAN 12 THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "twelve or more persons"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref Criminal Code s 67 (reading proclamation) (src:1084-1089)
GIVEN office IS A `s 67 office`
      `the person receives notice that, at a place within the person's jurisdiction, persons are unlawfully and riotously assembled together` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of persons the notice says are assembled` IS A NUMBER
      `the person has approached as near as is safe` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is satisfied that a riot is in progress` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67 the person must command silence and make the proclamation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 67 the person must go to that place` office `the person receives notice that, at a place within the person's jurisdiction, persons are unlawfully and riotously assembled together` `the number of persons the notice says are assembled` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty to go to the place has not arisen
        IF NOT `the person has approached as near as is safe` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "after approaching as near as is safe"
        IF NOT `the person is satisfied that a riot is in progress` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person is satisfied that a riot is in progress"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The proclamation itself, copied mechanically from the text ("in the following words or to the like effect").
-- src:1090 | Her Majesty the Queen charges and commands all persons being assembled immediately to disperse and peaceably to depart to their habitations or to their lawful business on the pain of being guilty of an offence for which, on conviction, they may be sentenced to imprisonment for life. GOD SAVE THE QUEEN.
@ref Criminal Code s 67 (the words of the proclamation) (src:1090)
`s 67 the words of the proclamation` MEANS "Her Majesty the Queen charges and commands all persons being assembled immediately to disperse and peaceably to depart to their habitations or to their lawful business on the pain of being guilty of an offence for which, on conviction, they may be sentenced to imprisonment for life. GOD SAVE THE QUEEN."

-- The duties as a regulative rule over the section's own offices: go to the place, then command silence and make the proclamation. The text states no time limit, so no WITHIN is invented.
-- src:1084 | Reading proclamation
-- src:1085 | 67 A person who is
-- src:1086 | (a) a justice, mayor or sheriff, or the lawful deputy of a mayor or sheriff,
-- src:1087 | (b) a warden or deputy warden of a prison, or
-- src:1088 | (c) the institutional head of a penitentiary, as those expressions are defined in subsection 2(1) of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act, or that person’s deputy,
-- src:1089 | who receives notice that, at any place within the jurisdiction of the person, twelve or more persons are unlawfully and riotously assembled together shall go to that place and, after approaching as near as is safe, if the person is satisfied that a riot is in progress, shall command silence and thereupon make or cause to be made in a loud voice a proclamation in the following words or to the like effect:
@ref Criminal Code s 67 (reading proclamation) (src:1084-1089)
DECLARE `s 67 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 67 goes to that place`
    `s 67 commands silence and makes, or causes to be made, the proclamation`

@ref Criminal Code s 67 (reading proclamation) (src:1084-1089)
GIVEN office IS A `s 67 office`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 67 office` `s 67 act`
`s 67 the duty of the person who receives notice` MEANS
    PARTY office
    MUST `s 67 goes to that place`
    HENCE (PARTY office
           MUST `s 67 commands silence and makes, or causes to be made, the proclamation`
           HENCE FULFILLED
           LEST BREACH BY office BECAUSE "s 67: the person did not command silence and make, or cause to be made, the proclamation")
    LEST BREACH BY office BECAUSE "s 67: the person did not go to the place"

§ `Section 68 -- Offences related to proclamation`

-- "Every one is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life who (a) opposes, hinders or assaults, wilfully and with force, a person who begins to make or is about to begin to make
-- or is making the proclamation referred to in section 67 so that it is not made; (b) does not peaceably disperse and depart from a place where the proclamation referred to in section 67 is made within
-- thirty minutes after it is made; or (c) does not depart from a place within thirty minutes when he has reasonable grounds to believe that the proclamation referred to in section 67 would have been made
-- in that place if some person had not opposed, hindered or assaulted, wilfully and with force, a person who would have made it."
-- Paragraph (c) names no moment from which the thirty minutes run: it is read from the moment the person has those reasonable grounds (fork F10).
-- src:1091 | Offences related to proclamation
-- src:1092 | 68 Every one is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life who
-- src:1093 | (a) opposes, hinders or assaults, wilfully and with force, a person who begins to make or is about to begin to make or is making the proclamation referred to in section 67 so that it is not made;
-- src:1094 | (b) does not peaceably disperse and depart from a place where the proclamation referred to in section 67 is made within thirty minutes after it is made; or
-- src:1095 | (c) does not depart from a place within thirty minutes when he has reasonable grounds to believe that the proclamation referred to in section 67 would have been made in that place if some person had not opposed, hindered or assaulted, wilfully and with force, a person who would have made it.
@ref Criminal Code s 68 (offences related to proclamation) (src:1091-1095)
DECLARE `s 68 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 68(a) opposes, hinders or assaults, wilfully and with force, a person who begins to make or is about to begin to make or is making the proclamation so that it is not made`
    `s 68(b) does not peaceably disperse and depart from a place where the proclamation is made within thirty minutes after it is made`
    `s 68(c) does not depart from a place within thirty minutes when he has reasonable grounds to believe that the proclamation would have been made in that place`
    `s 68 an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (c)`

@ref Criminal Code s 68 (offences related to proclamation) (src:1091-1095)
GIVEN act IS A `s 68 act`
      `the person opposes, hinders or assaults, wilfully and with force, a person who is making, or is about to begin to make, the proclamation referred to in section 67` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proclamation is not made as a result` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proclamation referred to in section 67 was made at the place where the person was` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has reasonable grounds to believe that the proclamation would have been made in that place if some person had not opposed, hindered or assaulted, wilfully and with force, a person who would have made it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the minutes since the proclamation was made (paragraph (b)) or since the person came to have those reasonable grounds (paragraph (c)), up to the person's peaceable departure or, if the person has not departed, up to now` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68 the person commits an offence related to the proclamation` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 68(a) opposes, hinders or assaults, wilfully and with force, a person who begins to make or is about to begin to make or is making the proclamation so that it is not made` THEN
        IF `the person opposes, hinders or assaults, wilfully and with force, a person who is making, or is about to begin to make, the proclamation referred to in section 67` AND `the proclamation is not made as a result`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "wilfully and with force" and "so that it is not made"
    WHEN `s 68(b) does not peaceably disperse and depart from a place where the proclamation is made within thirty minutes after it is made` THEN
        IF NOT `the proclamation referred to in section 67 was made at the place where the person was` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a place where the proclamation referred to in section 67 is made"
        ELSE IF `the minutes since the proclamation was made (paragraph (b)) or since the person came to have those reasonable grounds (paragraph (c)), up to the person's peaceable departure or, if the person has not departed, up to now` GREATER THAN 30
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within thirty minutes after it is made" (a period fixed in the text's own words: not exceeded)
    WHEN `s 68(c) does not depart from a place within thirty minutes when he has reasonable grounds to believe that the proclamation would have been made in that place` THEN
        IF NOT `the person has reasonable grounds to believe that the proclamation would have been made in that place if some person had not opposed, hindered or assaulted, wilfully and with force, a person who would have made it` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "when he has reasonable grounds to believe"
        ELSE IF `the minutes since the proclamation was made (paragraph (b)) or since the person came to have those reasonable grounds (paragraph (c)), up to the person's peaceable departure or, if the person has not departed, up to now` GREATER THAN 30
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within thirty minutes" (a period fixed in the text's own words: not exceeded)
    WHEN `s 68 an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (c)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Every one ... who (a) ... (b) ... or (c) ..."

