§ `Section 69 -- Neglect by peace officer`

-- "A peace officer who receives notice that there is a riot within their jurisdiction and, without reasonable excuse, fails to take all reasonable steps to suppress the riot is guilty of (a) an indictable
-- offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction." "Peace officer" is s 2's term (a seam input).
-- src:1096 | Neglect by peace officer
-- src:1097 | 69 A peace officer who receives notice that there is a riot within their jurisdiction and, without reasonable excuse, fails to take all reasonable steps to suppress the riot is guilty of
-- src:1098 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:1099 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 69 (neglect by peace officer) (src:1096-1099)
GIVEN `s 2 peace officer: the person is a peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person receives notice that there is a riot within their jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to take all reasonable steps to suppress the riot` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 69 the peace officer neglects to suppress a riot` MEANS
    IF `s 2 peace officer: the person is a peace officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        AND `the person receives notice that there is a riot within their jurisdiction`
        AND (NOT `the person has a reasonable excuse`)
        AND `the person fails to take all reasonable steps to suppress the riot`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A peace officer who receives notice that there is a riot within their jurisdiction and, without reasonable excuse, fails to take all reasonable steps to suppress the riot"

